  "finding_3_interpretation": "Under polynomial_n5: (Mg b, F) dA=+0.012 (still null, p=1.0); (Mg b, G) dA=-0.057, p=0.014 (still negative, attenuated from -0.21); (Mg b, K) dA=-0.035, p=0.020 (now negative, was null under production). The K-class effect emerges precisely because the continuum-level shortcut was removed.",
  "overall_interpretation": "The K-class shortcut composition is multi-leg. Under the production Gaia-ESO continuum: continuum level + FeI/CrI multiplets carry K-classification; Mg b is functionally redundant; (Mg b, K) returns null. Under polynomial_n5 re-derivation: continuum-level leg is destroyed; model leans on Mg b and FeI/CrI; (Mg b, K) recovers a measurable -0.034. Both results are evidence of shortcut learning; the audit detects the active leg under each continuum convention.",
